From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:58:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Load zlib as libz.so.1 on Linux

[DllImport("libz")] makes Linux look for libz.so, which only the zlib
development package installs, so a player without it crashed loading the UO
files. On Linux the assembly resolves "libz" to libz.so.1, which every system
has (ZLib.Linux.cs; ZLib.cs only calls it). Windows and macOS are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
---
 src/ClassicUO.Utility/ZLib.cs | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ClassicUO.Utility/ZLib.cs b/src/ClassicUO.Utility/ZLib.cs
index 5f5c39167..9eb31b219 100644
--- a/src/ClassicUO.Utility/ZLib.cs
+++ b/src/ClassicUO.Utility/ZLib.cs
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ using ClassicUO.Utility.Platforms;
 
 namespace ClassicUO.Utility
 {
-    public static class ZLib
+    public static partial class ZLib
     {
         // thanks ServUO :)
 
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ namespace ClassicUO.Utility
                 }
                 else
                 {
+                    UseVersionedLibzOnLinux();
                     _compressor = new CompressorUnix64();
                 }
             }
